{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST supply the review prompt that each group's reviewer follows. The prompt MUST direct the reviewer not to edit files. It MUST direct the reviewer to make mechanical changes itself in the revised text it returns, and to return design questions for the user.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has four obligations. The skill supplies a review prompt. The prompt directs the reviewer not to edit files. It directs the reviewer to make mechanical changes itself in the revised text it returns. It directs the reviewer to return design questions for the user.\n\nThe single test, `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_review_prompt_makes_mechanical_changes_and_returns_design_questions]`, covers all four:\n- **Supply:** the test reads the prompt through `review_prompt()`, which calls `skill_file(\"habeas-requirements\", \"references/review-prompt.md\")`. That lookup panics if the bundled skill has no such file. The files are embedded with `include_str!`, so the prompt has to ship with the skill.\n- **No file edits:** it asserts the prompt contains \"Don't edit files; make your changes in the revised text you return\". The prompt, `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/references/review-prompt.md`, has this sentence in its opening section.\n- **Mechanical changes:** it asserts the prompt contains \"**Mechanical changes:** make them yourself in the revised text, and never phrase them as questions\".\n- **Design questions:** it asserts the prompt contains \"**Design questions:** return these; the user decides\".\n\nThe test collapses whitespace first, so these phrases match across the prompt's line wraps. `assert_text` panics with the missing phrase if any is absent. Removing or reversing any of the three directives would fail the test.\n\nThe subject is a prompt-content requirement, so checking the prompt's wording is the right kind of test. Nothing the requirement states is left untested. There are no acknowledgments, and I found no gaps.",
  "references": "a1764fd961e7ff309b1190a1565f82dcbb9bd15698c40181c2ef1887c4f3d160",
